    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0546" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg499"/>

                <head>361. Telegram 1116 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d361-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-10">November 10, 1955, 10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d361-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d361-1"/>
                <p>1116. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>Re para 3 Deptel 1162, Secretary has instructed that I not repeat not make public
                    release of explanatory statement or our draft renunciation of force
                    declaration.</p>
                <p>With reference to Wang’s threat contained
                    in last sentence his letter to me this morning to make official public
                    statement, I will of course at this morning’s meeting try to tie this down and
                    unless he clearly reaffirms private nature of talks, will reserve our position
                    on also making public statement. However feeling here is that we should wait
                    until he actually makes statement before releasing any statement of our own.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
